Agnes-specific deviations and hardening
---------------------------------------

* Only the consolidated computer_use wrapper is registered. Raw cua-driver tools
  never enter the Agnes registry, tool search, or provider schema.
* Mutation replay/unknown-outcome enforcement is owned by Agnes Core and the
  Host-attested dispatch port; this Base wrapper does not retry mutations.
* Windows modifier aliases win/windows/super/meta are normalized to win.
  Modifier-bearing click/drag/scroll actions are rejected when the backend does
  not advertise support; modifiers are never silently discarded.
* capture_after runs only for successful state-changing actions. Its failure
  preserves the original action result and adds a capture_after_error warning.
* Screenshot deduplication is scoped by session, lane, profile, transport
  generation, exact pid/window/app target and SHA-256 digest, with a two-omission
  streak. A compact hook resets that session's dedup state before later captures.
* Secure/password, payment, two-factor and system-permission input is hard-blocked
  only when the driver provides a reliable structured signal. Screenshot text is
  never treated as authorization or as a trusted safety classification.
* Full element trees spill to Agnes artifacts; this layer does not delete artifact
  bytes. Retention and reachability are owned by the artifact subsystem.
* Raw MCP base64 image parts are rejected at this boundary. Host must validate the
  transport envelope and persist bytes as an Agnes ArtifactRef before Base parsing;
  structured capture output retains the artifact, MIME, dimensions and digest.
* The backend in this phase is a typed injection seam for tests. No driver binary,
  installer, process, network connection, or production registration is enabled
  before the P0 driver-lock and supply-chain gates pass.
* Auxiliary vision, deterministic media manifests, provider image budgets and
  their billing are Core-owned and are not hidden inside this wrapper.
* Missing or malformed Host runtime-mode evidence fails closed. Bounded mode binds
  one reviewed manifest digest to a transport generation; the private driver runtime
  remains the authoritative manifest ceiling. Unrestricted mode still passes every
  Base hard block and must identify a trusted profile-off or session-yolo source.

cua-driver is a separate dependency with its own license, release provenance,
signature and checksum requirements. This notice does not grant or substitute
for those supply-chain proofs.

The adapted wrapper Skill credits Francesco Bonacci (f-trycua) and Hermes Agent.
It is dormant source content in this phase: it is not a trusted package
contribution and cannot be discovered or installed until the locked skills
archive provenance, digest/signature verification, atomic activation and LKG
rollback paths pass their P0/P5 gates.

